{"answerable": true, "quotes": [{"source": "S1", "quote": "Item S-3.28.2: Size 230 x110 x150 cm.(for 20 users)"}, {"source": "S1", "quote": "Unit: Each | Rate: Rs. 35868.00"}, {"source": "S2", "quote": "Note :- Add or subtract proportionately for every 0.5 M increase or decrease in Length -12.5% Breadth & Depth -18 % each"}], "answer": "No RHB item lists a 20-user masonry septic tank 0.5 m longer than standard. The listed 20-user tank is Item S-3.28.2, "Size 230 x110 x150 cm.(for 20 users)", at Rs. 35868.00 per Each [S1]. This is a complete item rate, not a Chapter G basic rate. It covers construction of the septic tank with 40 cm masonry in CM 1:6, C.C bed, stone slab covering, plaster, foot rests, Ferro cement covers, earth work and disposal of surplus earth within 50 m [S1][S3].

The adjustment note is printed in the row for Item S-3.28.3, the 50-user tank. It says: "Add or subtract proportionately for every 0.5 M increase or decrease in Length -12.5% Breadth & Depth -18 % each" [S2]. The note is placed only under S-3.28.3, so the sources do not clearly state that it also applies to S-3.28.2 [S2][S3].

If the note is taken to apply to the 20-user tank, the tank would be 280 x 110 x 150 cm. The arithmetic is: 35868.00 × 12.5% = 4483.50, so 35868.00 + 4483.50 = Rs. 40351.50 per Each [S1][S2]. This is a derived figure, not a listed rate.", "missing": "The sources do not say whether the 0.5 m length-adjustment note (12.5%) under S-3.28.3 also applies to the 20-user item S-3.28.2. No rate is listed for a 280 cm long 20-user tank."}

